<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of Psalms</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Psalter</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of Psalms is a collection of 150 religious poems and songs in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a> and the Christian Old Testament, composed over several centuries and traditionally attributed in large part to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a>. Used in the worship of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Second Temple</a>, synagogue and church, the Psalms were among the first scriptures translated into many vernaculars, such as Dosoftei's Romanian verse Psalter of 1673.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/book-of-psalms.jpg" alt="Book of Psalms" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pete unseth · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Psalms_scroll.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
